    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald introduces to the market this superb three bedroom family home which has been recently redecorated and comes to the market in excellent condition with no onward chain. Offering exceptional space throughout, this will make an ideal purchase for both couples, or families alike and with its close proximity to UL could make an astute investment for parents with children of University age. \n\nIdeally positioned on the edge of the development opposite a green, the location could not be more convenient. With many amenities practically on the doorstep, including shops at City East business park and Groody Road, as well as restaurants, cafes and eateries and easy access to the city centre. The University of Limerick, Northern Trust, Bon Secours Hospital and The Plassey Technological Park, as well as access to the M7 Motorway are all within easy reach of the development.\n\nThe accommodation is bright and spacious, with a fresh interior which has only recently been repainted and new carpets laid. There is a living room on the immediate right after entering the hallway, with a feature fireplace providing the focal point. At the rear of the house is a large, open plan kitchen/dining room with access to the rear garden from sliding doors. There are three double bedrooms in the property with an ensuite showerroom in the main bedroom, as well as a family bathroom and guest WC on the ground floor. There are gardens at the front and the rear of the property with gated pedestrian side access.\n\nAccom: Ent. hall, guest WC, living room, kitchen/dining room, three bedrooms, ensuite, family bathroom."
      },
